%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 312e06c0a71026246afaeeda874120ba, type: 3}
  m_Name: Guide
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::Guide
  _guideItems:
  - sprite: {fileID: -855298285791758126, guid: c9d5ae2da6a463f448246bcdd8a481eb, type: 3}
    text: 'The game space is divided into 2 parts: the Screen and the environment.'
  - sprite: {fileID: 6937817954938267909, guid: 9ace197339531ee4eac942811f700ceb, type: 3}
    text: "There is the \u201Cgame\u201D on the screen, which has 4 elements: the
      timer, the tap, the slider, and the Pause button. Your task is to prevent the
      tap from filling up and the slider from running out before the timer ends.
      To do this, you need to click on the tap and drag the slider up."
  - sprite: {fileID: -6470460504253458178, guid: ce817694aeaa0b140acb8aa26b10e480, type: 3}
    text: "The Pause button pauses the \u201CGame\u201D."
  - sprite: {fileID: -4178046375966092550, guid: 359eb334261e3394f87a71f908b0856b, type: 3}
    text: The screen can also lag; if a lag occurs during the pause, the pause is
      lifted. When lagging, 10 seconds are added to the timer.
  - sprite: {fileID: 4130640169021434097, guid: e25968974f609ca4d9cf101dbc09c3f9, type: 3}
    text: "In the environment, there are 3 things to keep an eye on: the computer\u2019s
      battery overheats, and you need to turn on the fan to cool it down."
  - sprite: {fileID: 3465286685962602723, guid: b77a2cda28437cd489c21a366c8c6cb1, type: 3}
    text: And the Power Outlet, which periodically sparks and needs to be fixed with
      a click. Sparking increases the chance of computer lags.
  - sprite: {fileID: 7028616704906629411, guid: 30f39c9356081fa4a83ff28ba89e9d51, type: 3}
    text: The houseplant.
